{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"e604ff6ce69fdfba","name":"card_unit_chesire_regiment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Britain/BloodIron/units/card_unit_chesire_regiment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"CHESHIRE REGIMENT","text":"At the start of your turn, deal 2 damage to the enemy HQ if this unit was not attacked last turn.","flavorText":"The Cheshire Regiment was an infantry regiment of the Prince of Wales’s Division of the British Army, active from the year 1689 to 2007. During WWII the 2nd Battalion of the Cheshires first served in France in 1940 with the British Expeditionary Force, and was evacuated after the Battle of Dunkirk. The 2nd battalion then fought in North Africa from 1941 to 1943 and Sicily and Italy from 1943 to 1944. It landed in Normandy on D-Day and fought in the North West Europe campaign. The 1st Battalion fought at Tobruk in North Africa in 1941-1942 and later participated in the crossing of the Rhine in March 1945. The 6th and 7th Battalions fought in the Italian Campaign from 1943 to 1945. The 5th Battalion stayed in the UK throughout the war, where it provided machine gun support to the 38th Infantry (Reserve) Division, the 53rd (Welsh) Infantry Division, and the 80th Infantry (Reserve) Division.","faction":"Britain","type":"infantry","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":0,"defense":5},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_chesire_regiment","title":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_chesire_regiment_title","SourceString":"CHESHIRE REGIMENT","LocalizedString":"CHESHIRE REGIMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","defense":5,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Britain","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_chesire_regiment_text","SourceString":"At the start of your turn, deal 2 damage to the enemy HQ if this unit was not attacked last turn.","LocalizedString":"At the start of your turn, deal 2 damage to the enemy HQ if this unit was not attacked last turn."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_britain","Key":"card_unit_chesire_regiment_history","SourceString":"The Cheshire Regiment was an infantry regiment of the Prince of Wales’s Division of the British Army, active from the year 1689 to 2007. During WWII the 2nd Battalion of the Cheshires first served in France in 1940 with the British Expeditionary Force, and was evacuated after the Battle of Dunkirk. The 2nd battalion then fought in North Africa from 1941 to 1943 and Sicily and Italy from 1943 to 1944. It landed in Normandy on D-Day and fought in the North West Europe campaign. The 1st Battalion fought at Tobruk in North Africa in 1941-1942 and later participated in the crossing of the Rhine in March 1945. The 6th and 7th Battalions fought in the Italian Campaign from 1943 to 1945. The 5th Battalion stayed in the UK throughout the war, where it provided machine gun support to the 38th Infantry (Reserve) Division, the 53rd (Welsh) Infantry Division, and the 80th Infantry (Reserve) Division.","LocalizedString":"The Cheshire Regiment was an infantry regiment of the Prince of Wales’s Division of the British Army, active from the year 1689 to 2007. During WWII the 2nd Battalion of the Cheshires first served in France in 1940 with the British Expeditionary Force, and was evacuated after the Battle of Dunkirk. The 2nd battalion then fought in North Africa from 1941 to 1943 and Sicily and Italy from 1943 to 1944. It landed in Normandy on D-Day and fought in the North West Europe campaign. The 1st Battalion fought at Tobruk in North Africa in 1941-1942 and later participated in the crossing of the Rhine in March 1945. The 6th and 7th Battalions fought in the Italian Campaign from 1943 to 1945. The 5th Battalion stayed in the UK throughout the war, where it provided machine gun support to the 38th Infantry (Reserve) Division, the 53rd (Welsh) Infantry Division, and the 80th Infantry (Reserve) Division."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":